  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>One thing to know first</h2>
      <p>Le Lavandou and its surroundings remain one of the trickiest areas of the Var for swimming with dogs — most beaches here are closed to dogs in summer. On the other hand, several campsites in the area happily accept pets.</p>

      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Between Bormes-les-Mimosas and the Corniche des Maures, Le Lavandou's family campsites make a good base for exploring the Maures massif and its trails, even without a beach directly accessible with your dog.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>For a swim, you'll need to head to Bormes-les-Mimosas (a tolerated zone near Fort de Brégançon) or Cavalaire-sur-Mer, about twenty minutes by car.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the coastal path between Le Lavandou and Cavalière is walkable on a lead year-round, unlike the beaches.</div>
